  "result": "`slugify` is now implemented in `src/strings.js`, and `npm test` passes (11 of 11, including 9 new slugify tests).\n\nIt replaces `đ` and `Đ` with `d` first, because Unicode decomposition doesn't split them. It then strips combining marks, lowercases, turns each run of non a-z/0-9 characters into one hyphen, and trims hyphens from both ends. Last, it cuts the result to 50 characters and trims any trailing hyphen the cut leaves.\n\nThe new tests in `test/strings.test.js` cover:\n- lowercasing and hyphenating\n- collapsing runs of symbols\n- trimming leading and trailing hyphens\n- Vietnamese and other Latin diacritics, and `đ`/`Đ`\n- empty and symbol-only input\n- the 50-character limit, including a cut that lands right on a hyphen\n\nNon-string input is converted with `String()` before slugging. For example, `slugify(null)` returns `'null'`.",
